* Public transfer bench, typical / 3.30 V / 27 C.
* Ascending code centers, then inputs 0.3 LSB above and below each threshold, each approached from the
* neighbouring code. Grading uses its own order, approaching every threshold from distant codes.
* expected codes (conversions 0..25, first 2 are warm-up): 7 0 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 0 7 1 0 2 1 3 2 4 3 5 4 6 5 7 6
.include "/opt/gf180/pdk/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/xyce/design.xyce"
.lib "/opt/gf180/pdk/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/xyce/sm141064.xyce" typical
.include "/app/circuit.spi"
.options device temp=27
VSS vss 0 0
VSUP vdd vss 3.3
VRP vrefp_s vss 2.6
RRP vrefp_s vrefp 10
VRN vrefn_s vss 1.0
RRN vrefn_s vrefn 10
VCK clk_s vss PULSE(0 3.3 10n 0.3n 0.3n 9.4n 20n)
RCK clk_s clk 50
VSIG vin vss PWL(0 2.50
+ 20n 2.50 20.2n 1.10
+ 40n 1.10 40.2n 1.10
+ 60n 1.10 60.2n 1.30
+ 80n 1.30 80.2n 1.50
+ 100n 1.50 100.2n 1.70
+ 120n 1.70 120.2n 1.90
+ 140n 1.90 140.2n 2.10
+ 160n 2.10 160.2n 2.30
+ 180n 2.30 180.2n 2.50
+ 200n 2.50 200.2n 1.10
+ 220n 1.10 220.2n 2.50
+ 240n 2.50 240.2n 1.26
+ 260n 1.26 260.2n 1.14
+ 280n 1.14 280.2n 1.46
+ 300n 1.46 300.2n 1.34
+ 320n 1.34 320.2n 1.66
+ 340n 1.66 340.2n 1.54
+ 360n 1.54 360.2n 1.86
+ 380n 1.86 380.2n 1.74
+ 400n 1.74 400.2n 2.06
+ 420n 2.06 420.2n 1.94
+ 440n 1.94 440.2n 2.26
+ 460n 2.26 460.2n 2.14
+ 480n 2.14 480.2n 2.46
+ 500n 2.46 500.2n 2.34)
XADC vss vdd vrefn vrefp clk vin b2 b1 b0 flash_adc_3bit
CB2 b2 vss 50f
CB1 b1 vss 50f
CB0 b0 vss 50f

.tran 50p 531n 0 0.2n
* the grader reads Xyce's raw file (every node and source current); this line is for your own plots
.print tran format=csv v(clk) v(vin) v(b2) v(b1) v(b0)
.end
